From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: msm8998: clock the vcodec subcores

The decode session dies with a precise signature: the firmware answers
every control-plane packet (SYS_INIT, session create, LOAD_RESOURCES,
START) and then never completes a single EMPTY_BUFFER. Measured mid
-session via /dev/mem: SUBCORE0_GDSCR reads 0xa0282002 (powered) while
its CBCR reads 0x80006220 -- CLK_OFF set, enable bit CLEAR. The decoder
engine is powered and unclocked, so work queued to it never finishes.

Nothing ever enabled that clock. The vcodec-subcore patch that moved the
subcore power domains onto the parent also dropped .vcodec_clks_num to
zero, which turns every vcodec_clks_get()/enable() loop -- parent AND
per-session child -- into a no-op.

Complete the msm8939 pattern instead, which is the same V1/V3 power
model this SoC uses and is proven upstream: name the two subcore core
clocks on the parent node and restore vcodec_clks_num. core_power_v1()
then brings both subcore clocks up at every core power-on -- before the
firmware boots and probes its engines, which is when the vendor has
them up -- and the per-session vdec/venc child enables work again.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi    |  8 ++++++--
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -3183,9 +3183,12 @@
 				 <&mmcc VIDEO_AXI_CLK>,
 				 <&mmcc VIDEO_MAXI_CLK>,
 				 <&mmcc MNOC_AHB_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_MMSS_SYS_NOC_AXI_CLK>;
+				 <&gcc GCC_MMSS_SYS_NOC_AXI_CLK>,
+				 <&mmcc VIDEO_SUBCORE0_CLK>,
+				 <&mmcc VIDEO_SUBCORE1_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "core", "iface", "bus", "mbus",
-				      "mnoc_ahb", "noc_axi";
+				      "mnoc_ahb", "noc_axi",
+				      "vcodec0_core", "vcodec1_core";
 			iommus = <&mmss_smmu 0x400>,
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0x401>,
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0x40a>,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -893,6 +893,8 @@
 	.clks_num = 6,
 	.vcodec0_clks = { "core" },
 	.vcodec1_clks = { "core" },
+	.vcodec_clks = { "vcodec0_core", "vcodec1_core" },
+	.vcodec_clks_num = 2,
 	/*
 	 * Measured at the point of the wedge, with venus stopped just after
 	 * core_power(POWER_ON):
